    {
      "name": "Core",
      "hidden": false,
      "description": "serve                  Start the broker (syncs schema from protos; control plane on data-port+10).\ncatalog bootstrap      Give a project an ACTIVE catalog so an upgraded deployment can serve.\ncatalog stage          Stage the catalog built from your protos for a project, without activating it.\ncatalog activate       Make a staged catalog the project's ACTIVE one; running brokers reload it.\ncatalog status         Show the project's ACTIVE catalog (exit 3 when it has none).\nverify                 Compare the proto manifest against a LIVE database, read-only, before applying anything.\nenv                    Generate a working .env for a deployment posture, with real generated secrets.\nrequirements           Print the backend contract this project's manifest declares (run before first start).\ndoctor                 Env + backend readiness; --enterprise adds a manifest-aware prerequisite preflight."
    },
    {
      "name": "Diagnostics",
      "hidden": false,
      "description": "events tail            Print the events on a topic as JSON lines (optionally decoded).\nresources list         List the collections, graphs, indexes or buckets a backend holds.\ncompat-matrix          Print the authoritative supported proto-annotation matrix as JSON.\nexplain                Explain the generated DDL/DSN/policies for a message type.\nhealth-check           Lightweight Docker HEALTHCHECK — exit 0 if healthy.\ntracker-ddl            Emit the migration-ledger table DDL to stdout.\nconfig-skeleton        Emit a default MigrationOptions config skeleton as JSON."
    },
